  "hyp.h4": "They put the fridges behind a classic VPN or firewall.",
  "hyp.how4": "VPN and firewall login pages online in Europe; job ads that mention VPNs in EU retail, 32 days before vs after 12 Oct.",
  "hyp.found4": "Login pages −5%. VPN job ads flat (45 → 54, the same share of all ads).",
  "hyp.v4": "No sign",
  "hyp.h5": "They moved to zero-trust access (ZTNA: Zscaler, Cloudflare, Netskope, Barracuda…).",
  "hyp.how5": "EU retail job ads that mention ZTNA/SASE products; public DNS records of 49 large grocery chains in 14 countries; certificate logs for new remote-access hostnames.",
  "hyp.found5": "Job ads 8 → 6. DNS: 1 chain of 49 shows a ZTNA portal, and DNS can't say since when. Certificate logs (public logs reach only 23 Oct): 3 new remote-access-style names in the 11 days after the attack, none of them ZTNA, against 29 in the 32 days before.",
  "hyp.v5": "No sign",
  "hyp.h6": "Retailers started hiring for factory-style (OT) security.",
  "hyp.how6": "EU retail job ads that mention OT or industrial-control security.",
